    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d771">

                <pb facs="0839" n="827" sameAs="frus:frus1941v01/pg827"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">861.24/620</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum of Conversation, by the Secretary of
                        State</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1941-09-04">September 4, 1941</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>The Soviet Ambassador called at his request and talked at some length about the
                    failure of his Government to borrow any money from this country with the
                    exception of ten million dollars on gold collateral. I also expressed my regret
                    and disappointment in this respect and assured him that I would continue to do
                    my best to advance such matters, both as to credit and supplies for Soviet
                    Russia in the war. The Ambassador said that he made the mistake of his life in
                    agreeing not to accept lease-lend benefits and advantages instead of paying cash
                    or its equivalent for supplies in this country, and he mentioned how far behind
                    his country was in obtaining from this country most urgently needed military
                    supplies. I made appropriate reply to this and pledged every cooperation.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>C[<hi rendition="#small-caps">ordell</hi>] H[<hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >ull</hi>]</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
